.dev/

# Python bytecode caches — build detritus, not source. web/.gitignore already
# carries this for web/lcars_serve and web/tests; skills/lcars-xo/xo-report.py
# and its four siblings (xo-held.py, xo-logs.py, xo-criteria.py, xo-score.py)
# are Python too, and can produce the same detritus anywhere under skills/, so
# this is repo-wide rather than re-scoped per directory.
__pycache__/

# Test rigs — NOT in the product repo (captain's ruling, 2026-09-25):
#   "I don't want the test rigs checked into the LCARS repo at all. If they're
#    useful to have, put them in lcars-dev."
# They had reached 3,913 tracked files / ~109 MB, most of it recorded run
# output nobody realised was committed. The rig SCRIPTS now live in
# lcars-dev/tests/drives/; the recorded artefacts were untracked so live drives
# keep their evidence without the repo carrying it.
#
# WHERE THE ARTEFACTS ACTUALLY ARE (corrected 2026-09-29, S228 close-out).
# This block used to say they were "LEFT ON DISK here (untracking is not
# deleting)". That was true only of the machine that did the move: untracked
# files do not travel through `git push`, so a FRESH CLONE has no tests/drives/
# at all -- measured on the captain's new laptop three days later. The durable
# statement is that all 3,913 are still tracked in the PARENT of the commit that
# untracked them, and restore to the worktree without touching the index:
#
#   git archive 07e6b42^ tests/drives | tar -x -C .
#
# The ~2,600 that were on disk but never tracked did not survive, which is why
# claim-check 5a stays red (tests/drives/align-heal/runs/plain-1).
#
# This line is only the advisory half — it stops an accidental `git add`.
# `git add -f` walks straight past it, so tests/no-rigs.test.sh reads the real
# git index and FAILS the build if anything under here is tracked again.
#
# Shared EQUIPMENT that shipped suites in tests/*.test.sh source or exec is a
# different thing and is NOT ignored: it lives in tests/lib/ so a clone of
# LCARS stays testable (CLAUDE.md's golden rule).
tests/drives/
